== Effects ==
* Randomizes passive items and [[attribute]]s on pickup and at the start of every floor.
** Regarding stats, this randomness is not dependent on the run's [[Seeds|seed]].
** Stats gain a random modifier. These modifiers do not stack between levels and are instead rerolled every time.
*** [[Speed]] -0.2, 0 or +0.2.
**** {{dlc|nr}} Also affects maximum speed, may never exceed 2.0.
*** {{dlc|nr}} [[Range]] -0.5, 0 or +0.5.
*** {{dlc|r}} [[Range]] -2.5, 0 or +2.5.
*** {{dlc|nr}} [[Tears]] -0.5, 0 or +0.5.
*** {{dlc|r}} [[Fire rate]] -0.5, 0 or +0.5.
*** [[Shot speed]] -0.2, 0 or +0.2.
*** [[Damage]] flat -1, 0 or +1.
*** [[Luck]] -1, 0 or +1.
** Does not affect [[trinket]]s, [[card]]s, [[pill]]s, [[Pretty Fly|Pretty Flies]], {{i|The Polaroid}} / {{i|The Negative}}, {{i|Key Piece 1}} / {{i|Key Piece 2}}, {{i|Knife Piece 1}} / {{i|Knife Piece 2}}, or active items.

== Notes ==
* See {{i|D4}} for more details of the rerolling process.
* Due to losing all items every level, it is beneficial to try to gain permanent stat boosts if possible. These include using pills when equipped with {{i|PHD}} or {{i|Virgo}}, {{dlc|a+|sacrificing health with {{i|Potato Peeler}} to gain damage or {{i|Brittle Bones}} to gain tears,}} or using up {{i|Judas' Shadow}}.
* Like other full-reroll effects, Missing No. has a small chance to not reroll every item.
* {{Dlcalt|Can cause [[transformation]]s.|r=Transformations are lost when rerolling out of the items that caused them.}}
* Missing No. cannot be rerolled or removed by most means after being picked up, including:
** Rerolling passive items with {{i|D4}}.
*** A D4-type reroll will cause the stat modifiers from Missing No. to be rerolled. 
** {{dlc|a+|Using {{i|Clicker}} to remove the last item collected.}}
** {{dlc|r|Using {{p|XVII - The Stars?}} to remove the last item collected.}}
** {{dlc|r|Taking damage as {{c|Tainted Eden}} to reroll passive items.}}
* {{dlc|nr}} This item can be used to gain more [[health]] if desperately needed, as the randomization does often include items that grant you various types of hearts.
* {{dlc|nr}} If the player has already obtained a large number of items (such as during a run where they have gained infinite money in greed mode), it is highly recommended to avoid this item, as it will almost always end up rerolling all the items the player has thus far collected into {{i|Breakfast}}.<!-- Rerolling no longer breakfasts in Repentance. -->

== Synergies ==
* {{dlcalt|{{t|Butter!}}|r={{i|Genesis|dlc=n}}}}: Provide the only available methods for getting rid of Missing No.
** {{dlc|r|{{t|Butter!}} can no longer remove Missing No.}}
* {{I|Glowing Hourglass}}: Using Glowing Hourglass to go back to the previous floor will keep the rerolled items, which will allow to reroll them again.

== Interactions ==
* {{I|The Stairway}}: When getting the Stairway at the start of a floor, the ladder doesn't spawn. It will spawn at the start of the next floor even if rerolled.

